# mcp-skill-publisher Development Rules

## Environment Requirements
- Node.js >= 18.0.0
- npm >= 9.0.0
- Git 2.x+

## Code Style
- Use CommonJS (`require`/`module.exports`) for CLI compatibility
- Use `chalk` for all terminal output coloring
- Use `ora` for all spinner/progress indicators
- Error messages must suggest a remedy, not just report the error

## Project Conventions
- All source code in `src/`
- CLI entry point in `bin/cli.js`
- Templates in `templates/` with `.tpl` extension
- Skills (meta-skills for this tool) in `skills/`
- Configuration templates use `{{VARIABLE}}` placeholder syntax

## Disabled / Forbidden
- Do NOT use ES modules (`import`/`export`) in source — keep CommonJS
- Do NOT commit `node_modules/`
- Do NOT hardcode API keys or secrets
- Do NOT modify `package.json` version manually — use `npm version`

## Testing
- Unit tests alongside source: `src/**/*.test.js`
- Run all tests before commit: `npm test`
- Integration test: `node bin/cli.js publish --dry-run`
